=== prompt ===
Build LUMENFALL, a 2D action-platformer in Three.js inside this folder (orthographic camera, parallax 3D backing, low-res buffer upscaled + grain/vignette, Tenebris Somnia gritty pixel look). ES default + EN toggle, all HUD text from a strings table. Palette/style refs: 1.png (L1 emerald shrine), 2.jpg (L2 purple/toxic), 3.jpg (L3 burnt-orange/black). Character references in assets/: kael.jpeg (hero), statue.jpeg (Marble Mummy boss L1), goodwitch.jpeg (kind-elder disguise NPC L1), badwitch.jpeg (sorcerer Ul Burjo boss L2), demon.jpeg (antlered demon The Patient One boss L3) - side view only, flip horizontally for direction. Kael: light sword slash, jump, dash 0.2s w/ i-frames + ghost trail, 1 air dash, 1s cooldown; sword halo = only light in L3. Core mechanic L2: button rotates level group 90 degrees around player, 0.6s tween, gaps become bridges. Plot: sorcerer disguised as kind elder offers infinite wealth, steals village Ember to wake ancient demon; Kael returns it (green color-bleed ending payoff). Cutscenes: fullscreen panels + letterbox + typewriter. Enemy AI: sense->decide->act ticks, rolling model of last 20 player actions (dodge bias, aggression), counters bias + Easy/Normal/Hard scalar with fairness caps; L3 demon predicts lantern-light path. States: menu->cutscene->play->boss->...->ending. Static files only (index.html + js/ + css/). Backgrounds: 3 parallax layers per level from assets/bg/ (fallback: procedural gradient + silhouettes if missing).
